"""Nearly matched private-head budgets: width versus residual and depth.

Only cart/fav allocation changes. The inherited full random template is
initialized before fixed slicing/removal; click/buy Parameters, input masks,
losses and source-gradient ownership are retained. Shared dense clipping can
still couple private heads to optimized shared branches. These are replacement
controls with compensating widths, not a pure fixed-width factorial, and the
realized parameter budgets differ slightly. No empirical improvement is claimed.
